From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:50:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: skip a txq whose station is on the other hw

mt76_txq_schedule_list() takes the phy for each txq from its wcid. A
txq can outlive its station's wcid index on mac80211's active list: once
the index is freed, a station on the other band of a DBDC chip can get
it. The txq then came from band 0's hw while the phy was band 1's, and
mt76_txq_send_burst() dequeued it with ieee80211_tx_dequeue() on band
1's hw. mac80211's fq code then indexes one local's flows with the other
local's, which can corrupt memory.

Our earlier "schedule a station's txqs on the hw it belongs to" already
keeps ieee80211_next_txq() on the hw the round started on; skip a txq
whose wcid's phy is on another hw too. Multi-radio phys that share one
hw are unaffected.

Ported from pesa1234/openwrt next-r4.12.0.rss.mtk,
9999-18-wifi-mt76-fix-kernel-panic-in-tx-scheduling-on-dual-band-Wi-Fi-6
(Chen Minqiang). Not unit tested: this path needs mac80211's own txqs,
which the KUnit fakes don't have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index 67be2aa7..6a3e82bb 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -611,7 +611,15 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 		if (!wcid)
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * A stale txq whose wcid index now belongs to a station on
+		 * another hw (the other band of a DBDC chip): dequeueing it
+		 * there would mix the two hws' mac80211 queues.
+		 */
 		phy = mt76_dev_phy(dev, wcid->phy_idx);
+		if (phy->hw != hw)
+			continue;
+
 		if (test_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->state) || phy->offchannel)
 			continue;
 
